\f3 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f0\b\fs28 Eloise matters, but as a constraint rather than the motive\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f1 Your option 2 is useful, but I wouldn't make it the reason they come.\
Eloise has materially helped them. The manuscript explicitly has her 
\f0\b loaning military hardware/tanks to the Elvi
\f1\b0 , and she attends one of their major events under the pretext of supervising that hardware. So the Elvi have reason to regard her as something between ally, benefactor and terrifying arms-dealing grandmother.\
That means when they arrive, their position can initially be:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 protect Sarah; support Eloise; keep the UDF out.
\f1\b0 \
This is stronger than \'93we came to protect Eloise's interests,\'94 because the latter makes them subordinate to Shakti. They have their own political and religious interests by now.\
It also means the High Elvis can give very clear orders that 
\f0\b Shakti personnel are not enemies
\f1\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f0\b\fs28 Then why do they break Shakti security?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f1 Because the situation changes.\
This is where I think your musical-security idea becomes 
\f2\i more
\f1\i0  developmentally consistent, not less.\
The Elvi have repeatedly demonstrated an intrusive form of protection:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 We know what is best for the Holy Momma.\
When the final battle starts, Shakti security quite rationally locks Sublime Point down.\
From Eloise/Hayley's point of view:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Nobody gets in. Sarah stays protected inside.
\f1\b0 \
From the High Elvis's point of view:\

\f0\b The Holy Momma is trapped inside a compound under attack, nearing the sacred birth, while her followers are being kept outside.
\f1\b0 \
Those two perfectly reasonable positions become incompatible.\
The Elvi don't need to decide Eloise has betrayed them. They need only decide:\

\f0\b Shakti security is now preventing us from protecting Sarah.
\f1\b0 \
And they have precedent for ignoring the wishes of the protected person.\
So the stage goes to work.\
Importantly, 
\f0\b music is the ideal weapon against an ally
\f1\b0 , because they can disable Shakti security without shooting Shakti security personnel.\
That distinction matters.\
They aren't storming Eloise's compound with artillery. They're playing music until her extremely expensive security system has what may reasonably be described as a nervous breakdown.\
That feels much more like the Elvi.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f0\b\fs28 I would therefore make the development something like this\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f1 Initially:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 UDF surrounds Sublime Point.
\f1\b0 \
Then:\

\f0\b Elvi arrive and surround the UDF position / occupy approaches to the compound.
\f1\b0 \
Their declared purpose is essentially:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Nobody gets near the Holy Momma.\strokec2 \
That creates a bizarre situation in which 
\f0\b Eloise's enemies are besieging her, while an Elvis army is independently defending her from outside her own security perimeter
\f1\b0 .\
Eloise probably finds this tolerable because, tactically, free Elvis infantry is still free infantry.\
The stage contingent is permitted close to the Shakti gate precisely because 
\f0\b Shakti does not initially regard the Elvi as hostile
\f1\b0 .\
Then MoSES begins destroying UDF positions.\
The whole military geometry falls apart.\
The Elvi enter the fight against Fridge Force because:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Fridge Force starts threatening them;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 the MoSES attack is moving toward Sublime Point/Ruined Castle;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 the Elvi understand that something is now trying to reach the Holy Momma;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 and some of them are carrying the very Gyges discs Fridge Force wants.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Meanwhile the High Elvis wants people 
\f0\b inside
\f1\b0  the compound.\
Shakti security says no.\
And that's when:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 the stage turns toward the gate.
\f1\b0 \
That direction change is important.\
Until then the speakers have been facing outward, toward the UDF/road/battle.\
Now somebody turns the stacks around.\
That physical action alone tells the reader:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Oh. Eloise has just acquired another problem.\strokec2 \
Then the Elvi use the same musical trick already established elsewhere to destabilise the Shakti security system and open the gates.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f0\b\fs28 The developmental payoff\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f1 This also gives the Elvi a useful final progression.\
They began the novel largely as exploited entertainers.\
They became a religion.\
Then a political movement.\
Then a state.\
Then a military force.\
At Sublime Point, all those identities converge:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 religion:
\f1\b0  protect Holy Momma\uc0\u8232 
\f0\b politics:
\f1\b0  resist Dunhilton's government\uc0\u8232 
\f0\b military:
\f1\b0  fight the UDF/MoSES\uc0\u8232 
\f0\b culture:
\f1\b0  use music as an actual tactical weapon\uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Elvisness:
\f1\b0  do all of the above with stage equipment\
That's considerably more satisfying than having them attack the gate merely because you need the gate open.\
So I would preserve your security-disruption idea, but change its causal framing:\

\f0\b They do not come to Sublime Point intending to breach Shakti security.
\f1\b0 \
They come to 
\f0\b protect Sarah from the forces outside
\f1\b0 .\
Only during the collapse of the siege do they conclude that Shakti security itself is now 
\f0\b between them and Sarah
\f1\b0 .\
At that point, breaking in is entirely consistent with the Elvi's already-established, loving, reverent and profoundly disrespectful concept of personal protection.\
